<title>USA: Ashland says plans to develop Okwori South.</title>
<headline>Ashland says plans to develop Okwori South.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ashland Inc said Thursday its affiliate, Ashland Nigeria Exploration Unlimited, has declared the Okwori South Field commercial and plans to proceed with its development pending approval by the Nigerian authorities.</p>
<p>Ashland said it expects oil will be flowing from the field by July 1998 with an expected daily production of more than 20,000 barrels a day.</p>
<p>The field, owned jointly by Ashland and Total SA, is located about 40 miles offshore, in water about 450 feet deep.</p>
</text>
